  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "One, one, two, two.",
   "texto": [
    "In French all the names are masculine or feminine, and do not always match Spanish. **Un** is «un» and **une** is «a»: **un livre**, **une clé**. In plural, **des**: **des livres**.",
    "The defined article: **le** (el), **la** (la), **les** (los, las). In front of vowel or h muda, **le** and **la** become **l'**: **l'ordinateur**, **l'école**.",
    "The plural of many names is formed with **-s**, which is usually mute. In **le livre** / **les livres**, the difference is heard in the article."
   ]
